From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: OddBlueDog <3959851+OddBlueDog@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 21:27:47 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: mt7915: republish the global wcid after a full
 reset

mt76_reset_device() clears dev->wcid[], and mt7915_mac_full_reset()
only reallocated the global wcid's index without publishing it again,
unlike probe. Status requests for frames sent through the global wcid
were then reported as not acked and lookups for its index failed.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 mt7915/mac.c | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/mt7915/mac.c b/mt7915/mac.c
index e7be7ccd..1c7a36df 100644
--- a/mt7915/mac.c
+++ b/mt7915/mac.c
@@ -1516,6 +1516,8 @@ mt7915_mac_full_reset(struct mt7915_dev *dev)
 
 	i = mt76_wcid_alloc(dev->mt76.wcid_mask, MT7915_WTBL_STA);
 	dev->mt76.global_wcid.idx = i;
+	/* mt76_reset_device() unpublished it */
+	rcu_assign_pointer(dev->mt76.wcid[i], &dev->mt76.global_wcid);
 	dev->recovery.hw_full_reset = false;
 
 	mutex_unlock(&dev->mt76.mutex);
